nd that the Court is only allowed to consider arguments made in court and documents filed by actual parties to the case. They cannot ethically read or consider any other opinions or arguments about the case, and they cannot give legal advice. Thank you. Current Assignment Judicial Assistant Divisional Instructions Office Previous Assignments Education Current Assignment Circuit Judge: July 2017 – Present Alachua: Circuit Criminal Division I (A-E) Division V (Felony Forensics) Gilchrist: Criminal Cases Circuit-Wide: Jimmy Ryce Cases (including Alachua County Division “R”) Judicial Assistant Kayla Courtney courtneyk@circuit8.org Judge Wilson Bullard’s Division Procedures Court Reporting (PDF) Office Judge Stephan P. Mickle, Sr. Criminal Courthouse 220 South Main Street, Room A325 Gainesville, FL 32601 (352) 264-7057 Gilchrist County Courthouse 112 South Main Street Trenton, Florida 32693 Previous Assignments Alachua County Court Judge: January 2015 – June 2017 Alachua: Family Juvenile Delinquency CINS/FINS Truancy Levy: Circuit Civil Mortgage Foreclosures Extraordinary Writs Family Domestic Violence Probate Mental Health Juvenile Dependency Administrative Judge – Family Division, January 2025 – March 2026 Alachua: Family Division DR3 Alachua: Juvenile Delinquency Alachua: Family Division DV (Domestic Violence) Alachua: Division RP (Risk Protection) Alachua: CINS/FINS Alachua: Truancy Alachua County Children’s Trust Education Juris Doctor: University of Florida College of Law, 1990 Bachelor of Arts: University of Florida, 1986 Courts & Judges Court Calendars Jurors Departments & Services Self-Help Contact & Information Accessibility Policy Skip Navigation Courts & Judges Eighth Judicial Circuit About Administrative Judges Employment Circuit Judges Intranet (Restricted) Senior Judges Judicial Assignments General Magistrates and Hearing Officers Alachua County Baker County Bradford County Gilchrist County Levy County Union County About About About About About About Judic